oncerns:**\n- Multiple reports about Cursor having too many bugs\n- Performance issues with large codebases (can be slow or freeze)\n\n## Aider v0.56.0\n\n**Information Found:**\n- Aider is an AI pair programming assistant that operates in the terminal with LLM integration and Git support\n- Current version mentioned in documentation is v0.86.2, indicating v0.56.0 is an older release\n- There's a GitHub issue (#1507) about Windows installation difficulties with Aider v0.56.0\n- Installation available via pip: `pip install aider-chat`\n- The project writes approximately 70-80% of its own code according to commit history\n\n## Overall May 2026 Context\n\nThe AI coding tools landscape in May 2026 shows:\n- Intense competition between Claude Code, Cursor, and other AI editors\n- Many developers running multiple AI coding tools simultaneously\n- Cursor favored for daily inline edits, Claude Code for different workflows\n- Continued focus on bug fixes, performance improvements, and enhanced code review capabilities across all platforms"
